Z||000000||lowfunds||06-06-2001||06:22 PM||||Does anyone know of a replacement gasket for the 2.8? Called the autoparts store and the want $30.00 for a pair. I thought I read on the forum that the camaro gaskets will work, but could not find it in the search. Thanks for any help......||||reg||1
Z||000001||DecadenceR||06-06-2001||06:44 PM||||Also, which side of the heat shield on a 2.5 does the gasket go on?<BR>This may sound funny, but I forgot... LOL||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfiero||06-06-2001||08:51 PM||||Ask for exhaust manifold gaskets for a 1993-95 Camaro with the 3.4 V-6.  They are different looking, but work great (I have them on my GT).  The best part is the price.....$5 and some change. <P>The Fel-Pro part number is: MS 90864 ||||reg||1
Z||000003||PBJ||06-06-2001||08:52 PM||||I do believe the heat shield is agains the head and the gasket is against the manifold.||||reg||1
Z||000004||lowfunds||06-06-2001||08:52 PM||||sorry to take up space guys, did a search in the wrong forum section. Its been a long day. For anyone else that wants to know the 3.4 felpro high temp gaskets for a f-body will work.||||reg||1
